    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just \"sitting with emptiness.\" it's the realization that the song is over. i feel like a book that's already been read, kept on the shelf just out of habit. there's no more growth, no more impact. everything i was is gone, and what's left is just... waiting. is it really better to just drag out the process of fading away? does it even make sense to keep holding on when there's nothing left to hold onto?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
