      "content": "Your story didn't end because the pages are gone, but because there is space now for new chapters you write alone without expectation. Holding on doesn't prevent decay, but letting go of the old performance allows you to find rest instead of forcing a story that no longer fits. The point isn't to achieve growth anymore, but to find peace in being present even when everything feels silent and finished.",
